{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A multiline registered credential can be reconstructed in failure excerpts and sent to models, but such credentials are unusual in this configuration."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Output truncation can leave an unredacted credential fragment in saved gate output when a credential crosses the tail boundary."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The new assertions pass during ordinary test runs even when the supplied gate output is unredacted, so they do not verify redaction."}]}